//****************************************************************************
// $Module type: Class Package
// $Module name: cFTWebHtmlBox
// $Author     : Nils Svedmyr, RDC Tools International, <mailto:support@rdctools.com>
// Web-site    : http://www.rdctools.com
// Created     : 2026-07-02
//
// Description : FlexTron (FT) subclass of cWebHtmlBox: theme-aware behaviour for the FT
//               build. The HtmlBox renders in the FRAMEWORK DOM - style accordingly.
//
// This code is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY;
// without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
//****************************************************************************
Use cWebHtmlBox.pkg
Use seq_chnl.pkg               // Seq_New_Channel - the design-time dump below

// Drop-in for cWebHtmlBox that is marked NOT data-aware. The "Clear" toolbar button does
// `Broadcast Recursive Send Request_Clear of (Client_Id(ghoCommandBars))` (DFRefactorFT.src), which reaches
// EVERY web control in the client area. A bare cWebHtmlBox answers Request_Clear by delegating the DEO request
// to a server DEO it does not have -> GET_SERVERDEO -> Error 98 "Invalid message" (a whole series of them, on
// oWebShowAll_htm et al., when the Test Compile / output docks are open - Nils, LegacyApp 2026-07-02). DEO_Object
// False marks it non-data-aware so DEO-request broadcasts skip it (also covers Request_Save / Clear_All); the
// empty Request_Clear mirrors the sibling FT web controls (cFTWebButton et al.) as a guaranteed guard for the
// exact broadcast (a read-only HTML box has nothing to clear anyway). Otherwise identical to cWebHtmlBox.
// STAND-INS FOR THE DESIGNER (0.9.7). A box whose content is built when the program runs shows nothing in the Studio's
// Designer, which runs no code: it draws only a LITERAL psHtml. One short literal draws the content's shape instead -
// ftcontrols.css does the drawing: Set psHtml to '<div class="ftph-grid"><b>Name</b><b>Version</b></div>' is a grid
// with those two columns. There are a list, a tree, a log, a chart and cards too; the README's "Stand-ins for the
// Studio's Designer" lists them. Set the real content in End_Construct_Object, or when the dialog opens.
// Inherited from cWebHtmlBox; stated so the Designer models this class without the pooled package.
{ DesignerJSClass=df.WebHtmlBox }
// Clicks reach OnClick by default (Construct_Object below); the Studio's Properties panel shows the same default.
{ OverrideProperty=pbServerOnClick InitialValue=True }
/* THE DESIGN-TIME DUMP - a regeneration aid for the Designer placeholders, off by default.
   Every FlexTron dialog seeds its HTML boxes with an EXPRESSION at construct, which the Studio's
   Windows Designer cannot evaluate, so each box also carries a LITERAL copy of that markup for
   the Designer (2026-09-21). Those literals must be regenerated when a builder changes. A
   throwaway copy of the program sets gbFTDesignDump before any object constructs; every box is
   then remembered as it is built (gahoFTDesignBoxes), and once every object is built the program
   sends FTDesignDumpAll, which appends '<full object name>|<psHtml>' to gsFTDesignDumpFile for
   each - the exact string the runtime seeds, in the no-workspace state. The real program never
   sets the flag, so this costs one Boolean test per box.

   WRITTEN AT THE END, NOT AS EACH BOX FINISHES (2026-09-29). A box sets its runtime markup in its
   OWN End_Construct_Object, after "Forward Send End_Construct_Object" - so a dump written in this
   class's End_Construct_Object came too early, and held the design-time literal instead. */
Global_Variable Boolean gbFTDesignDump
Global_Variable String  gsFTDesignDumpFile
Global_Variable Handle[] gahoFTDesignBoxes
Move False to gbFTDesignDump
Move "" to gsFTDesignDumpFile

Class cFTWebHtmlBox is a cWebHtmlBox

    /* THE COLUMN DEFAULT, not a per-object decision. 47 of the 52 boxes in this app set
       piColumnIndex to 0 and the other five set 4, 8, 10 or 12 - so the value that was
       repeated 47 times is the default, and the five that differ override it exactly as
       they did when every site spelled it out. Behaviour-neutral: nothing loses a setting,
       47 lines stop restating one.

       CLICKS REACH OnClick BY DEFAULT (0.9.9), for the same reason: 22 of DFRefactor's 30 boxes
       set pbServerOnClick to True. It costs nothing on a box with nothing to click - the web
       engine sends a click to the server only when the clicked element, or one around it,
       carries data-ServerOnClick (WebHtmlBox.js). A box that must ignore such an element still
       sets it False.
    */
    Procedure Construct_Object
        Forward Send Construct_Object

        Set piColumnIndex to 0
        Set pbServerOnClick to True
        // The design-time dump: remembered now, written by FTDesignDumpAll once every object is built.
        If (gbFTDesignDump) ;
            Move Self to gahoFTDesignBoxes[-1]
    End_Procedure

    Function DEO_Object Returns Boolean
        Function_Return False
    End_Function

    Procedure Request_Clear
    End_Procedure

    // The live push, gated on the host page actually being ALIVE. UpdateHtml is a ClientAction
    // ("updateHtml") - delivered before the page's df.LocalApp has built its controls it breaks
    // the page, and the whole host renders the framework's "Unhandled Program Error on the
    // Client" banner (SelectFunctionsFT's Run-button bar, root-caused 2026-07-19: that view
    // mounts BEHIND the Folders view and WebView2 THROTTLES hidden windows, so the page can
    // still be initializing long after IsComObjectCreated turns True; a flaky cold-start
    // sighting on 2026-07-16 was the same race). pbInitWebApp of the owning
    // cLocalWebControlHost is the readiness truth - the framework flips it False on the page's
    // FIRST server call (FinishWebObjectInitialize). Until then, fold the push into Set psHtml:
    // the stored property is exactly what the page's init sync serves at mount, so nothing is
    // lost. ONE canonical home for the gate - the ~20 push sites need no per-site guards (the
    // gate at SelectFunctionsFT's oRunBtnDeferTimer stays: it also skips its CheckUpdateWebUI).
    // AppendHtml/UpdateHtmlArray share the ClientAction risk but have no callers - gate them
    // here too if they ever gain one.
    Procedure UpdateHtml String sHtml
        Handle  hoHost
        Boolean bInitializing
        Get Owner to hoHost
        Move False to bInitializing
        If (hoHost <> 0) ;
            Get pbInitWebApp of hoHost to bInitializing
        If (bInitializing = True) Begin
            Set psHtml to sHtml
            Procedure_Return
        End
        Forward Send UpdateHtml sHtml
    End_Procedure

End_Class

// The design-time dump (see gbFTDesignDump above): '<full object name>|<psHtml>' for every box, each with the markup
// it ended its construction with. Sent by the dump program once every object is built.
Procedure FTDesignDumpAll Global
    String sHtml
    Integer i iCh
    If ((gbFTDesignDump = False) or (gsFTDesignDumpFile = "")) ;
        Procedure_Return
    Move (Seq_New_Channel()) to iCh
    If (iCh < 0) ;
        Procedure_Return
    Append_Output channel iCh gsFTDesignDumpFile
    For i from 0 to (SizeOfArray(gahoFTDesignBoxes) - 1)
        Get psHtml of gahoFTDesignBoxes[i] to sHtml
        If (sHtml <> "") Begin
            Move (Replaces(Character(13), sHtml, "")) to sHtml
            Move (Replaces(Character(10), sHtml, "")) to sHtml
            Writeln channel iCh (Name(gahoFTDesignBoxes[i]) + "|" + sHtml)
        End
    Loop
    Close_Output channel iCh
    Send Seq_Release_Channel iCh
End_Procedure
